  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1242 AM CDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nNorthwesterly flow aloft is forecast to continue through much\nof the next week with some operational models showing a \ntransition to more zonal flow across the CONUS to end the \nnext week. Although there are numerous disturbances moving \nthrough the flow passing near to the area the next chance (20 to\n35%) for showers and storms appears to be late Tuesday night \nthrough Wednesday when a stronger shortwave moves across the\nregion. Rainfalls will be light with forecast probability of a\ntenth of an inch of rain or more near 0 percent. \n\nMonday is expected to be the coolest day of the period with high\ntemperatures in the mid to upper 70s and low temperatures in the\nmid to upper 50s. High temperatures the rest of the week are \nforecast to be in the lower to mid 80s. Monday night onward, \nlow temperatures are forecast to be in the lower to mid 60s.",
